# Release signing credentials — EXAMPLE ONLY.
#
# Do NOT copy this file over the project's gradle.properties. That file is
# tracked in Git now, so anything written there gets published.
#
# Signing credentials are read with project.findProperty, which resolves from
# your Gradle home as well as from the project. Use either of these instead:
#
# 1. Your personal, untracked Gradle home file — ~/.gradle/gradle.properties:
#
#        RELEASE_STORE_PASSWORD=your_store_password_here
#        RELEASE_KEY_ALIAS=your_key_alias_here
#        RELEASE_KEY_PASSWORD=your_key_password_here
#
# 2. Environment variables, which suit CI and never touch disk:
#
#        export ORG_GRADLE_PROJECT_RELEASE_STORE_PASSWORD=...
#        export ORG_GRADLE_PROJECT_RELEASE_KEY_ALIAS=...
#        export ORG_GRADLE_PROJECT_RELEASE_KEY_PASSWORD=...
#
# The keystore itself goes at the project root as opendroid-release.keystore.
# It is gitignored by the *.keystore rule and must stay that way.
#
# Without all three properties and the keystore file, release builds fail
# loudly rather than falling back to the publicly known debug key.
#
# Google account sync (D6) — OPTIONAL, same never-commit rule:
#
#        GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=123456789012-abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz123456.apps.googleusercontent.com
#
# This is the *Web application* OAuth client ID from your own Google Cloud
# project (the Android OAuth client for package com.opendroid.aiagent +
# your signing SHA-1 is registered in the same project but its ID is never
# pasted anywhere). Without it the app builds and runs normally; the Google
# account screen simply shows its setup-needed state. Full steps:
# feature-d6-report.md in the OpenDroid design workspace.
